    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is our clear headliner with an elite score of 82.05. Despite facing a formidable arm in Rod\u00f3n, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a strong lineup position and a platoon advantage that pushes him into \"must-start\" territory. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Crow, as **Luis Arraez** (69.53), **Jung Hoo Lee** (67.27), and **Matt Chapman** (64.59) all receive significant boosts from the favorable opposing pitcher xERA of 4.91. **Taylor Ward** remains a high-upside play at 65.63; while his dynamic platoon adjustment is slightly negative, the combination of leading off and beneficial wind conditions makes him an essential component of our offensive engine today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Daulton Varsho**, who fell to a 37.48 score primarily due to the severe challenge of facing Chris Sale. While **Daulton Varsho** brings necessary positional flexibility, the optimizer signaled a clear avoidance of Sale\u2019s elite strikeout profile to protect our batting average efficiency. Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.69) earns a spot in the MI slot by leveraging his assumed leadoff status, providing the necessary speed upside we prioritize in this 5x5 format. We are keeping a close eye on the confirmed lineups for **Will Smith**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, and **Lawrence Butler**; **Lawrence Butler** is currently the highest-risk play at 51.19, as he faces the stiff challenge of Shota Imanaga and carries a significant negative platoon adjustment. As **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** remain on the IL, and **Tyler Freeman** is off the board today, our depth will be tested, but we remain confident that our core of **Bryson Stott** (72.63) and the aforementioned standouts provides the best path to maximizing our daily efficiency.",
